# ── Generated dataset ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# transactions.csv is ~114 MB and graph_edges.csv ~40 MB at the current corpus
# size, past GitHub's 100 MB limit. The generator is the source of truth rather
# than the artefact:
#
# CAVEAT, because "deterministic (seed 42)" used to be claimed here and is not
# quite true: the STRUCTURE is deterministic, but complaint and legitimate-txn
# timestamps are stamped from an unseeded datetime.now(), so a rebuild differs in
# the timestamp column and everything derived from it (hour-of-day, the night
# penalty, the 120-minute live window). A given corpus is therefore NOT
# byte-recoverable once overwritten -- copy the two files aside before
# regenerating if the current one matters.
#
#     python scripts/generate_data.py
#
# The small CSVs stay tracked so the repo is inspectable without a full run.
data/transactions.csv
data/graph_edges.csv

# Screen recordings and scratch analysis output. The underscore-prefixed files
# are per-run diagnostics written by the evaluation scripts; the reproducible
# results they summarise live in data/metrics.json.
*.mp4
*.mov
data/_*.csv
data/_*.npy
# Scratch credential/alert stores written by the test harness, the smoke sweep
# and the stress pass. MULESHIELD_DB_PATH points them here so none of them can
# write an officer into the real store; none of them belongs in the repository.
data/_*.db
data/_*.db-wal
data/_*.db-shm

# Collected evidence. Real artefacts are victim and bank material; they belong
# in the deployment volume, never in the repository. The custody records live in
# the database, which is also ignored.
data/evidence/
data/_evstore/

# Isolated build used by scripts/smoke_ui.py. It points at a throwaway backend
# port, so it must never be served to anyone.
frontend/dist-smoke/

# Pitch material stays local. It is strategy, not source -- what we lead with,
# what we volunteer about our own weaknesses, and how we answer the questions we
# expect. Not something to publish while the competition is running.
docs/PITCH.md
docs/PROJECT_INVENTORY.md
docs/CONTEXT_HANDOFF.md
docs/MODEL_DEFENSE.md
docs/DISCUSSION_NOTES.md

# Superseded planning docs and UI-generator prompts. Kept locally, off GitHub.
docs/archive/

# Local project notes and internal PRD
PRD.md
prd.md
PRD_SUMMARY.md
prd_summary.md

# Officer credentials. Never commit this -- it holds password hashes and live
# session tokens, and a committed copy would put a working login for every
# deployment into a public repository.
muleshield.db
muleshield.db-wal
muleshield.db-shm
data/muleshield.db
data/muleshield.db-wal
data/muleshield.db-shm

# ── Pre-regeneration corpus archive ──────────────────────────────────────────
# transactions.csv and graph_edges.csv are gitignored AND not byte-reproducible
# (generate_data.py stamps complaint timestamps from an unseeded datetime.now()),
# so a regeneration cannot be undone by git alone. Anything experimenting with
# the corpus copies them here first. Local only -- never committed, 154 MB.
.archive/
